{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit Query can be used with server rendering by combining Lit SSR with TanStack Query Core hydration APIs re-exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-query"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The runnable source for this guide is the "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR example"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flow","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Flow"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server rendering has three phases:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a per-request "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefetch queries on the server and render Lit HTML with that client."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dehydrate the cache into the HTML, then hydrate a browser "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" before the client app renders."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Never share one server "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" between users or requests."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-prefetch-and-render","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Prefetch and Render"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { render } from '@lit-labs/ssr'\nimport { collectResult } from '@lit-labs/ssr/lib/render-result.js'\nimport { html } from 'lit'\nimport { QueryClient, dehydrate, noop } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\nimport { createDataQueryOptions } from './api.js'\nimport './app.js'\n\nasync function renderPage() {\n  const apiBaseUrl = 'https://example.com'\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient({\n    defaultOptions: {\n      queries: {\n        staleTime: 30_000,\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  await queryClient.query(createDataQueryOptions(apiBaseUrl)).catch(noop)\n\n  const appHtml = await collectResult(\n    render(\n      html`<ssr-app\n        api-base-url=${apiBaseUrl}\n        .queryClient=${queryClient}\n      ></ssr-app>`,\n    ),\n  )\n\n  const dehydratedState = dehydrate(queryClient)\n\n  return { appHtml, dehydratedState }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server passes the same client into the Lit element with a property binding. This lets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createQueryController"},{"type":"text","value":" read the prefetched cache during server render. If your query function calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":" during SSR, pass an absolute API origin instead of relying on a browser-relative URL."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client-hydration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client Hydration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import '@lit-labs/ssr-client/lit-element-hydrate-support.js'\nimport { QueryClient, hydrate, type DehydratedState } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      staleTime: 30_000,\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst dehydratedState = JSON.parse(\n  document.getElementById('__QUERY_STATE__')?.textContent ?? 'null',\n) as DehydratedState\n\nqueryClient.mount()\nhydrate(queryClient, dehydratedState)\n\nconst appElement = document.querySelector('ssr-app') as\n  (HTMLElement & { queryClient?: QueryClient }) | null\n\nif (!appElement) {\n  throw new Error('Expected the SSR app element to exist before hydration.')\n}\n\nappElement.queryClient = queryClient\nawait import('./app.js')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unmount the client when the page is unloaded if you mounted it manually:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"window.addEventListener(\n  'pagehide',\n  () => {\n    queryClient.unmount()\n  },\n  { once: true },\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"component-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Pattern"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The SSR example creates its controller only after a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" property is available:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  createQueryController,\n  type QueryClient,\n  type QueryResultAccessor,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-query'\nimport { createDataQueryOptions, type DataResponse } from './api.js'\n\nclass SsrApp extends LitElement {\n  static properties = {\n    apiBaseUrl: { attribute: 'api-base-url' },\n    queryClient: { attribute: false },\n  }\n\n  apiBaseUrl = ''\n  queryClient?: QueryClient\n  private dataQuery?: QueryResultAccessor<DataResponse, Error>\n\n  protected override willUpdate(): void {\n    if (!this.dataQuery && this.queryClient) {\n      this.dataQuery = createQueryController(\n        this,\n        createDataQueryOptions(this.apiBaseUrl),\n        this.queryClient,\n      )\n    }\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This explicit-client pattern is useful for SSR because the client is created by the renderer rather than discovered from a connected DOM provider."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"serialization","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Serialization"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embed dehydrated state as JSON in the HTML and escape characters that can break out of a script tag. The example server uses a small serializer before replacing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__QUERY_STATE_JSON__"},{"type":"text","value":" in the built HTML template."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit Query re-exports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" from TanStack Query Core. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydrate(queryClient)"},{"type":"text","value":" after server prefetching to capture the cache state. In the browser, parse that state, create a fresh "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":", call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrate(queryClient, dehydratedState)"},{"type":"text","value":", assign the client to the server-rendered element, and only then import the Lit component so it upgrades with the prefetched cache available."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"flow","text":"Flow","level":2},{"id":"server-prefetch-and-render","text":"Server Prefetch and Render","level":2},{"id":"client-hydration","text":"Client Hydration","level":2},{"id":"component-pattern","text":"Component Pattern","level":2},{"id":"serialization","text":"Serialization","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nLit Query can be used with server rendering by combining Lit SSR with TanStack Query Core hydration APIs re-exported from `@tanstack/lit-query`.\n\nThe runnable source for this guide is the [SSR example](../examples/ssr).\n\n## Flow\n\nServer rendering has three phases:\n\n1. Create a per-request `QueryClient`.\n2. Prefetch queries on the server and render Lit HTML with that client.\n3. Dehydrate the cache into the HTML, then hydrate a browser `QueryClient` before the client app renders.\n\nNever share one server `QueryClient` between users or requests.\n\n## Server Prefetch and Render\n\n```ts\nimport { render } from '@lit-labs/ssr'\nimport { collectResult } from '@lit-labs/ssr/lib/render-result.js'\nimport { html } from 'lit'\nimport { QueryClient, dehydrate, noop } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\nimport { createDataQueryOptions } from './api.js'\nimport './app.js'\n\nasync function renderPage() {\n  const apiBaseUrl = 'https://example.com'\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient({\n    defaultOptions: {\n      queries: {\n        staleTime: 30_000,\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  await queryClient.query(createDataQueryOptions(apiBaseUrl)).catch(noop)\n\n  const appHtml = await collectResult(\n    render(\n      html`<ssr-app\n        api-base-url=${apiBaseUrl}\n        .queryClient=${queryClient}\n      ></ssr-app>`,\n    ),\n  )\n\n  const dehydratedState = dehydrate(queryClient)\n\n  return { appHtml, dehydratedState }\n}\n```\n\nThe server passes the same client into the Lit element with a property binding. This lets `createQueryController` read the prefetched cache during server render. If your query function calls `fetch` during SSR, pass an absolute API origin instead of relying on a browser-relative URL.\n\n## Client Hydration\n\n```ts\nimport '@lit-labs/ssr-client/lit-element-hydrate-support.js'\nimport { QueryClient, hydrate, type DehydratedState } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      staleTime: 30_000,\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst dehydratedState = JSON.parse(\n  document.getElementById('__QUERY_STATE__')?.textContent ?? 'null',\n) as DehydratedState\n\nqueryClient.mount()\nhydrate(queryClient, dehydratedState)\n\nconst appElement = document.querySelector('ssr-app') as\n  (HTMLElement & { queryClient?: QueryClient }) | null\n\nif (!appElement) {\n  throw new Error('Expected the SSR app element to exist before hydration.')\n}\n\nappElement.queryClient = queryClient\nawait import('./app.js')\n```\n\nUnmount the client when the page is unloaded if you mounted it manually:\n\n```ts\nwindow.addEventListener(\n  'pagehide',\n  () => {\n    queryClient.unmount()\n  },\n  { once: true },\n)\n```\n\n## Component Pattern\n\nThe SSR example creates its controller only after a `queryClient` property is available:\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  createQueryController,\n  type QueryClient,\n  type QueryResultAccessor,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-query'\nimport { createDataQueryOptions, type DataResponse } from './api.js'\n\nclass SsrApp extends LitElement {\n  static properties = {\n    apiBaseUrl: { attribute: 'api-base-url' },\n    queryClient: { attribute: false },\n  }\n\n  apiBaseUrl = ''\n  queryClient?: QueryClient\n  private dataQuery?: QueryResultAccessor<DataResponse, Error>\n\n  protected override willUpdate(): void {\n    if (!this.dataQuery && this.queryClient) {\n      this.dataQuery = createQueryController(\n        this,\n        createDataQueryOptions(this.apiBaseUrl),\n        this.queryClient,\n      )\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis explicit-client pattern is useful for SSR because the client is created by the renderer rather than discovered from a connected DOM provider.\n\n## Serialization\n\nEmbed dehydrated state as JSON in the HTML and escape characters that can break out of a script tag. The example server uses a small serializer before replacing `__QUERY_STATE_JSON__` in the built HTML template.\n\nLit Query re-exports `dehydrate` and `hydrate` from TanStack Query Core. Use `dehydrate(queryClient)` after server prefetching to capture the cache state. In the browser, parse that state, create a fresh `QueryClient`, call `hydrate(queryClient, dehydratedState)`, assign the client to the server-rendered element, and only then import the Lit component so it upgrades with the prefetched cache available.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ssr\ntitle: Server Rendering & Hydration\n---\n\nLit Query can be used with server rendering by combining Lit SSR with TanStack Query Core hydration APIs re-exported from `@tanstack/lit-query`.\n\nThe runnable source for this guide is the [SSR example](../examples/ssr).\n\n## Flow\n\nServer rendering has three phases:\n\n1. Create a per-request `QueryClient`.\n2. Prefetch queries on the server and render Lit HTML with that client.\n3. Dehydrate the cache into the HTML, then hydrate a browser `QueryClient` before the client app renders.\n\nNever share one server `QueryClient` between users or requests.\n\n## Server Prefetch and Render\n\n```ts\nimport { render } from '@lit-labs/ssr'\nimport { collectResult } from '@lit-labs/ssr/lib/render-result.js'\nimport { html } from 'lit'\nimport { QueryClient, dehydrate, noop } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\nimport { createDataQueryOptions } from './api.js'\nimport './app.js'\n\nasync function renderPage() {\n  const apiBaseUrl = 'https://example.com'\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient({\n    defaultOptions: {\n      queries: {\n        staleTime: 30_000,\n      },\n    },\n  })\n\n  await queryClient.query(createDataQueryOptions(apiBaseUrl)).catch(noop)\n\n  const appHtml = await collectResult(\n    render(\n      html`<ssr-app\n        api-base-url=${apiBaseUrl}\n        .queryClient=${queryClient}\n      ></ssr-app>`,\n    ),\n  )\n\n  const dehydratedState = dehydrate(queryClient)\n\n  return { appHtml, dehydratedState }\n}\n```\n\nThe server passes the same client into the Lit element with a property binding. This lets `createQueryController` read the prefetched cache during server render. If your query function calls `fetch` during SSR, pass an absolute API origin instead of relying on a browser-relative URL.\n\n## Client Hydration\n\n```ts\nimport '@lit-labs/ssr-client/lit-element-hydrate-support.js'\nimport { QueryClient, hydrate, type DehydratedState } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      staleTime: 30_000,\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst dehydratedState = JSON.parse(\n  document.getElementById('__QUERY_STATE__')?.textContent ?? 'null',\n) as DehydratedState\n\nqueryClient.mount()\nhydrate(queryClient, dehydratedState)\n\nconst appElement = document.querySelector('ssr-app') as\n  (HTMLElement & { queryClient?: QueryClient }) | null\n\nif (!appElement) {\n  throw new Error('Expected the SSR app element to exist before hydration.')\n}\n\nappElement.queryClient = queryClient\nawait import('./app.js')\n```\n\nUnmount the client when the page is unloaded if you mounted it manually:\n\n```ts\nwindow.addEventListener(\n  'pagehide',\n  () => {\n    queryClient.unmount()\n  },\n  { once: true },\n)\n```\n\n## Component Pattern\n\nThe SSR example creates its controller only after a `queryClient` property is available:\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  createQueryController,\n  type QueryClient,\n  type QueryResultAccessor,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-query'\nimport { createDataQueryOptions, type DataResponse } from './api.js'\n\nclass SsrApp extends LitElement {\n  static properties = {\n    apiBaseUrl: { attribute: 'api-base-url' },\n    queryClient: { attribute: false },\n  }\n\n  apiBaseUrl = ''\n  queryClient?: QueryClient\n  private dataQuery?: QueryResultAccessor<DataResponse, Error>\n\n  protected override willUpdate(): void {\n    if (!this.dataQuery && this.queryClient) {\n      this.dataQuery = createQueryController(\n        this,\n        createDataQueryOptions(this.apiBaseUrl),\n        this.queryClient,\n      )\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis explicit-client pattern is useful for SSR because the client is created by the renderer rather than discovered from a connected DOM provider.\n\n## Serialization\n\nEmbed dehydrated state as JSON in the HTML and escape characters that can break out of a script tag. The example server uses a small serializer before replacing `__QUERY_STATE_JSON__` in the built HTML template.\n\nLit Query re-exports `dehydrate` and `hydrate` from TanStack Query Core. Use `dehydrate(queryClient)` after server prefetching to capture the cache state. In the browser, parse that state, create a fresh `QueryClient`, call `hydrate(queryClient, dehydratedState)`, assign the client to the server-rendered element, and only then import the Lit component so it upgrades with the prefetched cache available.\n"}
